{"name":"Rumours","hex":"#744245","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rumours","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of rumour"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of rumour"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rumours"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rumors (play)","blocks":[{"text":"Rumors is a farcical play by Neil Simon that premiered in 1988."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/29/Rumors_%28Neil_Simon_play_-_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rumors_(play)"},{"title":"Rumors (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Rumors is the third album by the American band Arrogance, released in 1976. It was their first album on a major label, Vanguard Records. In 2000, Don Dixon re-released all of Arrogance's albums on his own label, Dixon Archival Records. The version of \"Rumors\" contained two bonus tracks, demos of \"Open Window\" and \"Final Nickel\" recorded at Charlotte's Reflection Sound Studios in 1975."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6a/Arrogancerumors.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rumors_(album)"},{"title":"Rumours (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Rumours is the eleventh studio album by the British and American rock band Fleetwood Mac, released on 4 February 1977, by Warner Bros. Records. Largely recorded in California in 1976, it was produced by the band with Ken Caillat and Richard Dashut. The recording sessions took place as the band members dealt with breakups with one another and struggled with heavy drug use, both of which shaped the album's direction and lyrics."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fb/FMacRumours.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rumours_(album)"},{"title":"Rumours (2024 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Rumours is a 2024 comedy horror film written and directed by Guy Maddin, Evan Johnson, and Galen Johnson. The film stars Cate Blanchett, Charles Dance, Roy Dupuis, Denis Ménochet, Nikki Amuka-Bird, Rolando Ravello, Takehiro Hira, Zlatko Burić, and Alicia Vikander."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/1b/Rumours_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rumours_(2024_film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/29/Rumors_%28Neil_Simon_play_-_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/29/Rumors_%28Neil_Simon_play_-_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARumors.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Fleetwood_Mac_Billboard_1977.jpg/500px-Fleetwood_Mac_Billboard_1977.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Fleetwood_Mac_Billboard_1977.jpg/500px-Fleetwood_Mac_Billboard_1977.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fleetwood Mac in 1977. From left to right: Mick Fleetwood, Christine McVie, John McVie, Stevie Nicks and Lindsey Buckingham.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFleetwood_Mac_Billboard_1977.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/The_Plant_-_Sausalito_-_front_door_2.jpg/500px-The_Plant_-_Sausalito_-_front_door_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/The_Plant_-_Sausalito_-_front_door_2.jpg/500px-The_Plant_-_Sausalito_-_front_door_2.jpg?utm_source=